# TermLaunch is a Windows-only project built with MSVC and edited in Visual
# Studio, so the working tree is CRLF everywhere. Git still stores LF in the
# repository; these rules make that consistent on every clone regardless of the
# cloner's core.autocrlf setting.

#* text=auto eol=crlf

# The generated tray icons are binary. Never let a line-ending filter near them
# — a single byte of conversion corrupts the DIB rows and the icon renders
# blank or upside-down. Regenerate with tools/make-icons.ps1 if that happens.
*.ico binary

# Session files read and written by the app are ASCII with LF endings and no
# BOM (PuTTY/KiTTY format). None are checked in today, but if a sample or test
# fixture ever is, it must keep LF or the terminal will not parse it.
Sessions/** -text
*.session text eol=lf
